# ACT ONE

.COLD OPEN

A ticking clock in the dark. Then silence.

EXT. CENTRAL STATION - NIGHT #1#

= Mara misses the last train and meets Leo.

Rain hammers the glass roof. MARA (30s, soaked, a cello case on her back) runs across the empty concourse.

The departures board flips: LAST TRAIN - DEPARTED.

MARA
(out of breath)
No. No, no, no.

LEO (O.S.)
It left four minutes early.

[[Leo should already be in frame, half hidden by the pillar.]]

She turns. LEO (60s, night guard, thermos in hand) steps out of the shadow.

LEO (CONT'D)
It always does on Thursdays.

CUT TO:

INT. GUARD BOOTH - CONTINUOUS #2#

A tiny room: a heater, a radio, a chessboard mid-game.

MARA ^
Is there a bus?

LEO ^
There is me, and there is tea.

/* An alternative line we cut:
LEO
Buses are for quitters.
*/

int. guard booth - later

They play chess. The radio murmurs the weather.

EXT. PLATFORM 4 – DAWN #3A#

The first train glides in, empty and gold in the low sun.

!MARA LOOKS BACK.

The booth is dark. Leo is gone. Only the thermos is left on the bench.

> FADE OUT.
